    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tI direct a small nonprofit that runs evening digital-literacy workshops for adults.\ne002\tA community center across town, Willow Hub, wants us to start a second site in autumn.\ne003\tTheir neighborhood has very little free support, and our mission is access.\ne004\tBut our current site is inconsistent: some nights we have thirty participants, some nights twelve, and volunteer coverage is fragile.\ne005\tI cannot tell whether expansion would force us to become better or expose that the first site is not actually stable.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne006\tExpansion will not automatically create discipline; it can just duplicate uncertainty.\ne007\tBefore committing, I would separate demand, delivery capacity, and what you mean by a successful site.\ne008\tWillow Hub's interest establishes a possible channel, not yet reliable attendance or staffing.\ne009\tIf the current variation comes from scheduling or outreach, a second location might help.\ne010\tIf it comes from an unclear program or exhausted volunteers, another site could magnify it.",
